The Query Farm modifications, also released under the BSD 3-Clause License,
add support required by the Vector Gateway Interface (VGI) Arrow IPC wire
protocol:

  * Per-record-batch custom_metadata (Arrow IPC Message field 4) encode +
    decode, surfaced on decoded tables via `_vgiRecordMetadata` /
    `_vgiRecordMetadataPerBatch`.
  * Multi-batch IPC stream encoding: `tablesToIPC` and `concatTables`,
    preserving per-table batch positions even when some tables are
    metadata-only (zero column-data batches).
  * Empty-record-batch synthesis for metadata-only batches on a non-empty
    schema (e.g. VGI EXCEPTION batches).
  * Foreign Arrow type acceptance in the encoder (arrow-js `isSigned` /
    `ArrayType` shapes), enabling columns built from arrow-js DataTypes to
    serialize through flechette.
